{
  "description": "Waggle v1 rule-matching cases (WAGGLE.md, 'Rule matching'), shared by the waggle Python library and the Wiggins Android client so both matchers agree. Each case gives the phone's rules (WAGGLE.md rule objects, as in waggle.capabilities), an optional 'unmatched' mode ('block' or 'ask'; absent means the WAGGLE.md default, 'block'), and the data of a waggle.intent. 'expect.mode' is the decision; 'expect.rule' is the 0-based index into 'rules' of the rule that decided, or null when no rule matched and 'unmatched' applied. No case has two rules that tie on both specificity and mode, so the deciding rule is unique.",
